hexagon: run the KV cache rotation as a fast Walsh-Hadamard transform
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-htp

The defect

A quantized KV cache makes llama.cpp rotate Q, K and V with a Hadamard matrix
(llama_mul_mat_hadamard), and the attention output back. Each rotation is a
MUL_MAT with the hint GGML_HINT_SRC0_IS_HADAMARD. The CPU, CUDA, Metal, Vulkan
and SYCL backends run a fast Walsh-Hadamard transform (FWHT) for such a
MUL_MAT and do not read the matrix. HTP0 multiplied by the full matrix: on the
phone the rotations of one decode token took 226 us (2B) and 382 us (4B).

The change

The host sends a hinted MUL_MAT as the DSP op HTP_OP_FWHT (htp/fwht-ops.c)
when src1 and dst are F32 with packed rows of 64, 128 or 256 values. The op
does not read src0. It multiplies each row by 1/sqrt(n), then it does the
butterflies in the sequence of ggml_compute_forward_fwht_f32, thus with IEEE
adds each value is the value of the CPU transform. A stage in one vector (1 to
16 values) gets the partner of each lane with one vdelta and selects the sum
or the difference with a lane mask. A stage across vectors adds and subtracts
full vectors. Groups of 16 vectors (2 rows of 256, 4 rows of 128, 8 rows of 64)
stay in the registers. With less than 256 rows the op uses one thread.

Rows of 64 values always go to the op. Rows of 128 or 256 values go to the
op to a maximum of 8192 values (32 rows of 256). The per-op profile of the
phone gives the limit: for rows of 256 values the op takes 2 to 13 us from 2
to 32 rows, against 8 to 19 us for the MUL_MAT, and from 64 rows the HMX
MUL_MAT is faster (17.5 against 19 us at 64 rows, 452 against 594 us at 8192
rows). For rows of 64 values the op is as fast or faster at each measured
count (8 to 65536 rows). Thus a decode step runs each rotation as the op, and
a prefill block runs the rotation of Q and K as the MUL_MAT. A different
MUL_MAT stays HTP_OP_MUL_MAT.

supports_op accepts each MUL_MAT that the op takes, with no VTCM check,
because the op uses no VTCM. ggml_hexagon_rows_packed requires the strides
that the op requires: ggml_is_contiguous permits any stride for a dimension
of size 1, and the op refuses such a descriptor with HTP_STATUS_NO_SUPPORT.
The op also refuses a dst with a different row count.

test-backend-ops gets six MUL_MAT_HADAMARD cases: a pair of rows of 256 and
one more row, 32 and 33 rows of 256 (the two sides of the limit), a group of
4 rows of 128 and 3 more rows, a group of 8 rows of 64 and 5 more rows, and
300 rows of 64 for more than one thread.

The results

The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, target fwht, the release flags, one thread)
gives 363 cycles for a row of 256 values and 87 for a row of 64 on v79
(timing mode). On v79 and v81 each value is equal to the value of the CPU
transform. On v73 and v75 the adds give qf32 values: 24800 of 35840 values
differ from the CPU transform, and the largest error is 3.5e-7 of the largest
value of a row, against 1.3e-7 for the f32 CPU transform (functional mode,
the error against a float64 transform).

On the phone (HTP0, a build of this op with no row limit, 2026-09-23 and
2026-09-24), the rotations of one decode token take 104 us (2B) and 212 us
(4B), against 226 and 382 us for the MUL_MAT. A greedy generation of the 2B
and of the 4B with a Q8_0 K and V cache gives the correct answer. The KL of
the 64 decode rows against the naive x86 oracle is 0.000807 for the 2B at
4096 tokens (F16 cache 0.000745), 0.000931 at 16384 (0.001053), and for the
4B 0.000545 at 4096 (0.000565) and 0.000667 at 16384 (0.000696).

On the phone with this patch (HTP0, 2026-09-24, the library set of the
series with this patch): test-backend-ops gives 15 of 15 MUL_MAT_HADAMARD
cases against the CPU. A greedy generation of the 4B with a Q8_0 K and V
cache and flash attention in AUTO mode gives the correct answer. The KL of
the 4B at 4096 tokens against the naive x86 oracle is 0.000510 for all rows
and 0.000542 for the 64 decode rows. The profile of the 4B (1024 prompt
tokens, 8 decode tokens) has 288 rotations, 272 of them as HTP_OP_FWHT: each
decode rotation, and V and the attention output of the prefill.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

